thinproxy (0.2.7-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * Fix the build on Linux architectures other than x86_64 and aarch64:
    the seccomp SIGSYS handler was compiled but unused there, so
    -Wall -Werror rejected it and the daemon would not build at all.
  * Initialize err in handle_connecting and zero the accept address so no
    uninitialized stack bytes are read or copied into the connection.
  * Report the actual failing syscall (setgroups/setgid/setuid) in the
    drop_privs privileged branch instead of always logging "setuid".
  * Add printf format attributes to logmsg and buf_appendf so -Wformat
    checks their call sites.

 -- Renaud Allard <renaud@allard.it>  Tue, 07 Jul 2026 10:39:14 +0200

thinproxy (0.2.6-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * Tear down a relay connection as soon as no descriptor remains that
    can drain its buffers, instead of holding the slot, descriptors and
    per-IP count until the idle reaper fires. This covers a relay whose
    descriptors are both closed with undeliverable data still queued and
    one whose descriptors are both hung up and parked.
  * Gate the parked-descriptor read re-arm on the EOF flag so a finished
    direction is not re-armed for a reader that no longer exists.

 -- Renaud Allard <renaud@allard.it>  Tue, 07 Jul 2026 08:47:51 +0200

thinproxy (0.2.5-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * Track live connections in a list so a relay whose client fd was torn
    down is still idle-reaped and counted against the per-IP limit,
    fixing a connection-slot leak introduced in 0.2.4 that let one source
    exhaust max_connections and wedge the listener.
  * Park a hung-up relay descriptor that cannot be drained because the
    far buffer is full, instead of busy-looping the event loop on its
    sticky POLLHUP; it is re-armed once the buffer drains.
  * Handle a relay transport error before the read and write handlers so
    data already buffered toward the surviving peer is flushed on a reset
    rather than discarded.
  * Harden build_request snprintf accounting against a negative return,
    report an inverted strtonum range as invalid, and include stdint.h.

 -- Renaud Allard <renaud@allard.it>  Mon, 06 Jul 2026 19:52:44 +0200

thinproxy (0.2.4-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * Drain a half-closed relay socket before signalling EOF so a full
    buffer no longer truncates the forwarded stream.
  * Close descriptors that have hung up or taken a transport error
    instead of leaving them in the poll set, which spun the event loop
    at full CPU until the peer drained or the connection timed out.
  * Replace the client Host header with the request-target authority on
    forwarded requests (RFC 7230 5.4) and accept a request without a
    Host, giving it the synthesized one.
  * Strip the URI fragment from the forwarded request-target.
  * Match access-control rules written in IPv4-mapped form
    (::ffff:a.b.c.d).
  * Unwrap an operator NAT64 prefix inside fc00::/7 or fec0::/10 and
    block private IPv4 embedded in Teredo and ISATAP addresses.
  * Honor -V regardless of config validity and reject an empty -u
    argument that would have silently skipped the privilege drop.
  * Align the strtonum and closefrom compatibility shims with their
    OpenBSD semantics.

 -- Renaud Allard <renaud@allard.it>  Mon, 06 Jul 2026 17:35:48 +0200

thinproxy (0.2.3-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * Replace the snprintf-based strlcpy shim with a real bounded copy so
    -Werror builds succeed below -O2 and under BSD make.
  * Allow restart_syscall in the seccomp filter so a stopped and resumed
    daemon (SIGSTOP/SIGCONT, container pause) is not killed on x86_64.
  * Flush buffered relay data to the surviving peer before closing on a
    transport error instead of discarding it.
  * Add the -F flag to force foreground, overriding a daemon yes setting;
    the systemd unit uses it.
  * Validate the HTTP version token in the request line.
  * Stop folding a URL query or fragment into the hostname and forward it
    in the path instead.
  * Require a single run of digits for Content-Length.
  * Require a valid IPv6 literal inside brackets in the request target.
  * Block more IANA special-use ranges in deny_private (192.0.0.0/24,
    198.18.0.0/15, fec0::/10, TEST-NETs, 6to4 relay anycast).
  * Reject a non-regular config file and report read errors instead of
    treating them as end of file.
  * Reject config lines containing a NUL byte and values with embedded
    whitespace.
  * Require the /96 suffix on nat64_prefix as documented.
  * Honor idle_timeout values shorter than the poll interval.
  * Do not idle-reap a connection while its DNS resolution is in flight,
    bounding the number of resolver children.
  * Select the init script by target OS instead of probing the build host
    and install the man page under PREFIX/man on OpenBSD.
  * Reject rcctl reload in the OpenBSD rc.d script.
  * Run the systemd service as an unprivileged DynamicUser and raise
    LimitNOFILE.

 -- Renaud Allard <renaud@allard.it>  Thu, 11 Jun 2026 12:32:58 +0000

thinproxy (0.2.2-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * Block IPv4-compatible and 6to4 IPv6 addresses that embed a private
    IPv4 destination, closing a deny_private SSRF bypass.
  * Reject whitespace in the request-target.
  * Reject forwarded requests that lack a Host header.
  * Accept a maximal-length configuration line ending in a newline.
  * Set optreset before the second getopt scan on BSD.
  * Preserve the reverse direction of a half-closed CONNECT tunnel on
    the SO_SPLICE path.
  * Fix a format-truncation build error on DragonFlyBSD.

